# PIMID (1.12.109): a 1T1R RRAM cell (one CMOS access transistor per cell), the RRAM cell of NVMExplorer
# (Pentecost, Hankin, Donato, Hempstead, Wei, Brooks, HPCA 2022; repository data/cell_cfgs/RRAM.cell and
# cell_cfgs.py RRAMCellConfig defaults): 53 F^2 and a 6 F access transistor, its reference cell being
# derived from TSMC's N40 1T1R macro (Chou et al., ISSCC 2018). The resistances, read and SET/RESET
# values are NVSim's sample_RRAM.cell values, as that repository states. Every published 22-40 nm RRAM
# macro (TSMC N40 and N22, Intel 22FFL) is 1T1R.
-MemCellType: memristor

-CellArea (F^2): 53
-CellAspectRatio: 1

-ResistanceOnAtSetVoltage (ohm): 100000
-ResistanceOffAtSetVoltage (ohm): 10000000
-ResistanceOnAtResetVoltage (ohm): 100000
-ResistanceOffAtResetVoltage (ohm): 10000000
-ResistanceOnAtReadVoltage (ohm): 1000000
-ResistanceOffAtReadVoltage (ohm): 10000000
-ResistanceOnAtHalfResetVoltage (ohm): 500000

-CapacitanceOn (F): 1e-16
-CapacitanceOff (F): 1e-16

-ReadMode: current
-ReadVoltage (V): 0.4
-ReadPower (uW): 0.16

-ResetMode: voltage
-ResetVoltage (V): 2.0
-ResetPulse (ns): 10
-ResetEnergy (pJ): 0.6

-SetMode: voltage
-SetVoltage (V): 2.0
-SetPulse (ns): 10
-SetEnergy (pJ): 0.6

-AccessType: CMOS
-AccessCMOSWidth (F): 6

-ReadFloating: false
